  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "The line 'Transfer to City of Grand Island - payments in lieu of taxes' is printed as a positive 104,077 and the statement's change in net position (1,167,061) adds it, although the label says it is a payment to the City (FY2023 prints it negative). Is the sign a misprint?",
      "amount": 104077,
      "recorded_as": "business_type.transfers_net +104,077 as printed (statement ties with the positive sign)",
      "source_page": 3
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Entirely business-type (Water Department of the City of Grand Island), GAAP, 2022 column (only column printed). Receipts and disbursements from the Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p3); no single total printed, so business-type totals are computed (operating + nonoperating). Debt issuance costs and Gain on disposal are dashes. transfers_net = 'Transfer to City of Grand Island - payments in lieu of taxes' printed 104,077 without parentheses; the statement's own math adds it (operating income 375,989 - 112,041 + 104,077 + 799,036 = 1,167,061), so it is recorded positive as printed (see decision_needed). other_financing = Capital contributions 799,036. 69,788,369 + 6,949,447 - 6,685,499 + 104,077 + 799,036 = 70,955,430. Balance sheet from Statement of Net Position (pp1-2); closing line misprinted 'Total assets and deferred outflows of resources' 77,350,080 = liabilities 6,394,650 + net position 70,955,430. Other revenue kept as other (no statement shows it counted in charges for services). Proprietary cash flows from p4. No detail schedules in the trimmed PDF. Read pages 1-4 of 4"
}
